<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01348#juxtaposition_of_images> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The image juxtaposes two distinct scenes: the top half showing sheep with their rear ends facing forward, and the bottom half showing men in traditional attire reacting with exaggerated expressions. This juxtaposition is central to the meme's intent and humor."@en .
_:Nf3ad9e21676d47f38b7567ec8b28c247 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
_:Ne0574c9690504d5a89f02f6684933187 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:Nf3c61342ab4a49fc93c70f4f3c2824f4 .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01274#mapping_001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The top text 'how you guys think you looks like' maps the viewer's self-perception onto the visual entity of the man. The man's ordinary appearance (scruffy beard, beanie, leather jacket) is used to represent how the viewer perceives themselves as looking, contrasting with the implied perception of 'pados wale pandit jee'."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01359#text_chunk_1> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#extractedFrom> "01359.png" .
