<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01327#mapping_001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The text 'i'm not sick, i'm twisted' and 'sick makes it sound like there's a cure' is presented as a monologue or statement from the speaker, who is visually represented by the Joker character. The visual material of the Joker is used to embody the speaker's identity and the ironic message. The Joker's menacing, twisted persona is directly mapped onto the textual claim of being 'twisted' rather than 'sick', creating an analogical mapping where the visual entity (Joker) serves as the embodiment of the speaker's self-identification."@en .
