<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#geometricallyAdjacentTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> _:Na6b94ec86f6542edb13190d499b25095 .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01324#assertion_about_01324> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general#hasToxicityExplanation> "The meme creates a harmful juxtaposition by labeling ordinary-looking men as 'the great train robbers', which could trivialize or misrepresent real historical criminals. While the intent is humorous, the mapping can be seen as potentially harmful by reducing complex historical figures to a comedic stereotype, which may disrespect the victims or the gravity of the event."@en .
_:Nb665b3d4817d4fd2b41f7f903e112344 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:N14cade2a79374c709fa1294737abdeb8 .
_:N1fc2b16fbbcf44cabd53c4d92c56bd79 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:N57ab56fdc8b04bc6b658b4cf3ed33f89 .
_:Ne60a8d1c815a40dc863dcf1f6135727c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01359#mapping_3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The text 'let me in' is overlaid on the image of the metal gate, visually mapping the gate as the physical barrier that the 'Naruto Runners' are trying to breach, thus representing the literal 'let me in' request."@en .
_:N404511aecea34c688b802fc065f6316f <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:N03144f879dec45849e2c991d712ed744 .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01524#concealed_weapon_threat> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The image of a person concealing a handgun behind their hip is a visual trope often associated with danger, aggression, or impending violence. This is a common cinematic and media representation used to signal a threat, and understanding this visual convention is necessary to interpret the meme's implied escalation of conflict."@en .
