_:Nc13b165ea99f43b2b6e113c3b609327e <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01483#audience_id> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme is designed for a broad online audience that understands irony and is familiar with cultural expectations around religious settings. The humor relies on the contrast between the solemnity of a mosque and the mundane idea of boredom, which requires general cultural knowledge about religious practices. The target audience is likely individuals who recognize the stereotype of Muslims being depicted as bored or unengaged, even if the image itself does not explicitly show such a stereotype. The meme's effectiveness depends on the viewer's awareness of the irony and the cultural context of religious gatherings, making it accessible to those who are familiar with these concepts."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01459#fear> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The woman's facial expression, with wide eyes and an open mouth, combined with her raised hands near her head and crouched posture, clearly conveys intense fear. This is amplified by the visual context of being surrounded by numerous spiders, which triggers arachnophobia."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01275#assertion_about_01275> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general#asserts> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01275#Black_man_in_a_suit_shouting_at_press_conference> .
