<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01476#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the visual material of the woman with prosthetic arms, who serves as a direct embodiment of the message 'im confident in my own skin'. The text explicitly refers to 'my own skin', which deictically anchors the message to the viewer's own identity. The woman's confident pose, self-assured expression, and visible prosthetic arms function as a visual model or mirror for the user, inviting them to project their own self-acceptance onto her. The projection is not deictic in the grammatical sense (e.g., 'you' or 'me' in the text), but it is semiotic: the user is invited to identify with the woman as a representation of the ideal self described in the text. The woman is the 'me' in the text, and the user is encouraged to see themselves in her, making her the projected entity."@en .
