<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#DramaticIrony> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01452#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: the_feeling_after_a_long_day_at_work_chimp; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The scene depicts a chimpanzee sitting on grass in a relaxed, slightly slumped posture, with one arm draped over its body and the other resting on its knee, conveying a sense of exhaustion or resignation. The text overlay reads 'the feeling after a long day at work,' creating an analogical mapping where the chimp's weary demeanor is humorously equated to human fatigue from work. The meme's intent is to evoke relatable humor by anthropomorphizing the chimp's posture as a universal symbol of post-work exhaustion. There is no toxicity present. The image does not contain any abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or propagandistic content. The chimp is used as a neutral, non-human subject to represent a common human experience, avoiding any stereotyping or harmful association. The visual elements (chimp, grass, posture) are not paired with any markers that could activate harmful stereotypes, as the chimp is not depicted with any cultural, racial, gendered, or religious markers that would imply a stereotype. The meme relies on the universal relatability of work fatigue and the comedic juxtaposition of a chimp's posture with human work-life experiences, without targeting any specific group or causing harm."@en .
_:N1986589019dd4e0bb662577963c5189e <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualMaterial> .
