<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01359#semiotic_projection_2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the metal gate, which represents the physical barrier they are humorously trying to breach. The text 'let me in' overlaid on the gate invites the user to imagine themselves as the one pleading to enter, aligning with the meme's satirical narrative of fictional characters attempting to access a restricted area."@en .
