<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01527#knee_injury_or_pain> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The gesture of holding the knee is a common visual trope used to imply injury or pain, especially in the context of physical activity like running. This is a real-world concept that helps interpret the visual cue, but is not directly visible as a medical diagnosis."@en .
