<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01465#hateful_divisiveness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The emotion expressed is one of hatred and division, stemming from the text 'there is difference between violating muslims and other muslims' and 'dont get confused'. This text promotes a false dichotomy and encourages hostility or violence against Muslims by suggesting a distinction between 'violating' and 'other' Muslims, which is a harmful and inflammatory message. The emotion is conveyed through the manipulative and misleading nature of the text, which aims to sow discord and normalize prejudice."@en .
