_:N56614649dfa84bb09b138209bedd44ea <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01324#historical_1960s_british_culture> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The cultural context of 1960s Britain, including media portrayals of crime and the public's fascination with notorious criminals. The Great Train Robbery was a major news story at the time and became a cultural touchstone. The meme references this era's cultural memory, which is necessary to understand the significance of the label 'the great train robbers'. The black-and-white photograph style also evokes the documentary or newsreel aesthetic of that period, enhancing the historical reference."@en .
