<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01392#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the visual material of the girl, who is depicted as the one speaking into the phone. The text 'hello jesus' and 'thanks for making a way!' are interpreted as being spoken by the girl, creating an implicit 'you' or 'me' projection where the viewer identifies with the girl's action of calling Jesus. This is a common meme structure where the viewer sees themselves in the role of the central character performing the action described by the text. The projection is onto the VisualMaterial entity 'girl' as the agent of the invocation."@en .
