_:N1fd0d857a2f747bf8d3a9b23d8d55bb0 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01487#mapping_forget_retarded> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The overlaid text 'when you forget you're retarded' creates an analogical mapping where the visual entity (the woman holding the sign) is implicitly identified as the subject of the insult — the person who forgets. The meme projects the textual concept of 'forgetting' onto the visual subject, and the derogatory label 'retarded' is applied to her as a consequence. This mapping is established through the juxtaposition of the text with the visual material, where the woman's neutral/surprised expression and the context of a public event are used to frame her as the target of the insult. The mapping is abusive and relies on the visual subject being equated with the textual insult."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01526#retail_store_environment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The background, though blurred, implies a retail store setting. This knowledge is necessary to understand the context of the transaction. The meme's humor is derived from the incongruity between the mundane retail environment and the absurd text overlay."@en .
