<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01258#stereotype_of_men_as_heteronormative_or_homophobic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme relies on the stereotype that men are expected to be heteronormative and intolerant of behaviors that challenge traditional gender roles or sexual norms. The label "@en .
_:N9a0b4c40ec114b74a6c002371587f267 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualMaterial> .
_:Nffed310d14104847a2455d3484932593 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01423#nap> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A nap is a short period of sleep, typically taken during the day, often for rest or recovery. The term is commonly used to describe a brief, informal sleep break, especially after a long day of work or activity. The background knowledge required to understand the meme is that 'nap' implies a desired state of rest and relaxation, which contrasts with the implied physical exertion of 'mudding'."@en .
_:N85d33bc737f841efb63348068890839a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:Nef115220a6314483834f3b834a8a0e9f .
_:Nf0a88096b6f84a49aa564ab043637598 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01468#assertion_about_01468> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general#asserts> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01468#assad> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01349#historical_event_Nazi_Germany> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The totalitarian regime led by Adolf Hitler from 1933 to 1945, characterized by extreme nationalism, racial persecution, and the implementation of the Holocaust. The regime's ideology and actions are the foundation for the historical condemnation of Hitler. The meme's use of his image in a sanitized context is a form of historical revisionism that distorts this legacy."@en .
_:N7dfe481a6f504cdd8be018db1ed5868b <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01269#religious_identity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme is designed to target the Muslim community by using the text 'definitely not a Muslim' in juxtaposition with Kermit the Frog, a non-Muslim fictional character, to mock or dismiss Muslims. The intent is to ridicule or belittle this religious group by associating them with a cartoon character, which is a form of cultural or religious mockery."@en .
_:N0b087e91d0dc461abb469eac6b07e6a1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01395#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the text overlay 'i just found out mexican babies come out just like the food', which uses first-person language ('i just found out') to create an implicit 'you' or 'me' perspective. The user is invited to identify with the speaker of the text, imagining themselves as the one who made this discovery, thereby projecting themselves onto the textual material. This projection is reinforced by the visual of childbirth, which serves as a dramatic backdrop for the user to imagine themselves in the context of the joke."@en .
_:N5fd34615fc3344cfa089a54ad21eb32b <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualMaterial> .
