_:Nd24d102838ca4b079a957366be3d8f39 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01456#Textual_reference_to_music_culture> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The text overlay 'they see them rollin.....' and 'they hating...' is a reference to the hip-hop culture and the song 'Rollin' by the group 'The Game' and '50 Cent', which is often used in memes to express a sense of defiance or to highlight a contrast between two groups. This reference is outside the image and requires external knowledge to understand the meme's cultural context."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01243#dog_praise_culture> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme targets individuals who are familiar with the common cultural practice of pet owners praising their dogs with phrases like 'good girl' or 'good boy' as a form of positive reinforcement. This cultural reference is central to the humor and relatability of the meme, making it most effective for audiences who have experienced or observed this interaction in human-animal relationships, particularly in Western cultures where dogs are often anthropomorphized and treated as family members."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01472#individual_autonomy> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#extractionTimestamp> "2025-12-12T02:45:38.314831" .
