<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01382#pro_choice_movement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A political and social movement advocating for the right to abortion and reproductive autonomy. The phrase 'my body my choice' is a hallmark slogan of this movement. The meme uses this slogan to assert a pro-choice stance, while the visual of erasing 'Abortion' creates a paradoxical or provocative message, suggesting that the act of erasing the word is itself a form of rejecting the concept, which is contrary to the pro-choice message."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01247#satire> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A literary, dramatic, or artistic work that uses humor, irony, exaggeration, or ridicule to criticize and expose the absurdities or vices of individuals, institutions, or society. The meme is a form of satire that critiques racism by using a shocking juxtaposition to make a point about the nature of prejudice."@en .
