<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01236#terrorism> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The use of violence or threats of violence to intimidate or coerce governments, organizations, or populations, often for political or ideological purposes. The meme uses the real-world concept of terrorism to create a harmful stereotype by associating it with sexualized and vulgar behavior, which is both inaccurate and dehumanizing. This association is offensive and contributes to a hostile environment by normalizing harmful attitudes against a specific group."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01256#sadness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The dog's facial expression, characterized by large, droopy eyes with visible tear, a slightly downturned mouth, and a generally melancholic appearance, conveys a strong sense of sadness. This is amplified by the tight framing on the dog's face, which emphasizes its emotive features."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01467#assertion_about_01467> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general#hasToxicityExplanation> "The meme uses the juxtaposition of a positive, celebratory visual (happy man, thumbs up) with a racially charged, offensive term to create a harmful and hateful message. The intent is to demean and dehumanize white people by associating them with a pejorative label, which constitutes hateful content under the specified toxicity categories."@en .
