<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01236#audience_id> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme is designed for an audience familiar with internet meme culture, particularly those who understand the 'sheep butts' meme and the satirical juxtaposition of images. The target audience likely includes individuals who find humor in crude, offensive, and exaggerated stereotypes, particularly those who may hold or be exposed to harmful views about ISIS or Middle Eastern communities. The meme relies on cultural references to strip clubs and ISIS, which may resonate with audiences who are aware of or interested in politically charged or satirical content, even if it is toxic. The visual elements (men in traditional attire, exaggerated shock expressions) are used to evoke a reaction from viewers who recognize these as markers of Middle Eastern or Muslim identity, making the meme's target community those who are either familiar with or indifferent to the harmful stereotypes it promotes."@en .
