<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01276#concept_smile_worth_thousand_words> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This is a common English idiom that conveys the idea that a simple, genuine smile can communicate more emotion, understanding, or goodwill than lengthy verbal explanations. It is used to emphasize the power of non-verbal communication and emotional expression. The idiom is culturally ingrained in Western societies and is often used in contexts promoting empathy, positivity, and human connection."@en .
