<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01527#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the visual material of the person holding their knee, as the text 'oh no i can't run anymore' creates a relatable scenario. The user identifies with the physical struggle depicted, imagining themselves in that situation. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you' in the text, but the implicit 'I' is strongly implied by the universal, first-person experience of physical exhaustion during exercise, which the meme is designed to evoke."@en .
