<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01456#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the meme as a whole, interpreting the juxtaposition of the Nazi leaders' parade and the prisoners behind barbed wire through the lens of the text overlay 'they see them rollin.....' and 'they hating...'. The text 'they' is a deictic pronoun that implicitly refers to the viewer/user, who is positioned as the observer of the contrast. The user is thus projected onto the textual material (the text chunks) and the visual material (the scenes) to understand the meme's message. The user is not explicitly projected onto a single entity but onto the entire meme structure, which includes both the visual and textual components."@en .
