<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01379#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the visual entity 'white_american_teenage_girl' through the implicit framing of the meme. The text 'american teenage girl' explicitly labels the subject, and the overall intent of the meme (as described in the context) encourages the viewer to identify with or empathize with the 'American teenage girl' as the active agent performing the 'visit'. This creates a semiotic projection where the user is positioned as the 'American teenage girl' or as someone who embodies her role in the narrative, even if not explicitly stated with deictic pronouns. The user is projected onto the visual material entity 'white_american_teenage_girl'."@en .
