<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01275#man> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A Black man with short dark hair and a goatee, wearing a dark pinstripe suit, white shirt, and light blue tie. He is depicted shouting aggressively with his mouth open and one hand raised in a pointing gesture, conveying anger or defiance. His facial expression is intense, with furrowed brows and a strained look, emphasizing the confrontational nature of the scene."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01269#kermit_the_frog_character> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Kermit the Frog is a fictional character from the Muppet franchise, created by Jim Henson. His widely recognized image is used in the meme to contrast with the text 'definitely not a Muslim'. Understanding that Kermit is a fictional, non-human character is essential to interpreting the meme's satirical or mocking intent."@en .
