<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01382#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the textual material 'my body my choice' because this phrase is the central assertion of personal autonomy and choice, directly addressing the viewer's identity as a person who holds this right. The visual of erasing 'Abortion' serves as a contrasting action, but the text explicitly frames the user as the holder of this right, making the user the subject of the claim. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me' in the text, but the phrase 'my body my choice' inherently implies the user's personal ownership and agency, projecting the user onto the slogan as its rightful owner and advocate."@en .
