<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01459#assertion_about_01459> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general#hasToxicityExplanation> "The meme uses the visual of a person in fear of spiders (arachnophobia) to create a humorous or ironic juxtaposition with the absurd claim that all spiders are terrorists. While the humor stems from the absurdity of the claim, the text 'they're re all terrorists' could be interpreted as promoting a harmful stereotype of labeling entire groups as inherently dangerous or evil, even when applied to non-human entities. This could potentially normalize or trivialize the serious concept of terrorism by associating it with a common fear, which may be seen as insensitive or harmful in certain contexts."@en .
