<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01469#concept_gas_mask_as_protection_from_toxic_substances> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#relatedTo> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01469#soldier> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01268#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: father_and_daughter_bonding_time_is_the_best; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The scene depicts a warm, affectionate embrace between an elderly Muslim man (wearing a kippah and glasses) and a younger Muslim woman (wearing a hijab), both smiling joyfully while seated on a couch. The visual elements include religious markers (kippah, hijab) and a familial interaction set in a neutral, domestic environment. There are no visible signs of toxicity such as abusive language, cyberbullying, harmful stereotypes, hateful content, misogyny, or propaganda. The overall intent of the meme is to promote positive family bonding, specifically between a father and daughter, and to encourage viewers to like and share the image if they agree with the sentiment. The intent is to evoke feelings of warmth, familial love, and cultural pride, using the visual of a loving Muslim family to reinforce a positive message about intergenerational relationships and religious identity. The meme functions as a sentimental and aspirational piece, aiming to resonate with audiences who value family time and cultural traditions."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01395#childbirth_pain_stereotype> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The image of a woman in labor screaming in pain is used to amplify the shock value of the stereotype. This is a common visual trope in media to represent childbirth as an extreme, almost violent, physical ordeal, which is then juxtaposed with the offensive text to heighten the absurdity and crudeness of the joke."@en .
_:Ncc9a6937077144aab4be97c7c36fb36d <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:N59009ddd5bfc4c2d903c364c24a7d91c .
_:Nebf7b675a2d042e8803ca0be9c15b33d <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:N210e5edc7eec4ce2a47bef2cf906448a .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01483#irony_as_a_comic_device> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#relatedTo> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01483#bored_people_in_mosque> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01247#Holocaust> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The systematic, state-sponsored persecution and murder of six million Jews by Nazi Germany and its collaborators during World War II. It is the most notorious example of genocide in history and is directly linked to the ideology of racism and anti-Semitism promoted by the Nazi regime."@en .
