<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01389#mapping_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The top text 'confession-every sunday around brunch time' is mapped onto the visual entity 'person', implying that the person is the one performing the 'confession' ritual. The person's affectionate interaction with the cat visually represents the 'confession' activity described in the text."@en .
_:N4e890540a39a44feb218aa9d17964080 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01276#mapping_smile_worth_words> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The textual phrase 'a smile is worth a thousand words' is mapped onto the visual entity of the smiling child. The child's joyful expression serves as the visual instantiation of the 'smile' mentioned in the text, and the entire scene visually represents the concept that this non-verbal expression carries more weight than words. The mapping is established through the direct juxtaposition of the text with the child's smile, which is the focal point of the image."@en .
