_:Nc2ee9bccaf5d48958b5ad26795fc4a42 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01284#mapping_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The text 'muslims offend me' is juxtaposed with the visual of a person wearing a pig mask and holding a pig figurine. This creates an analogical mapping where the person in the visual material (wearing the pig mask) is being used to represent or stand in for 'muslims' as described in the text. The pig mask and figurine serve as visual symbols that map onto the textual concept of 'muslims', creating a harmful stereotype that equates Muslims with pigs or pig-like behavior. This mapping is central to the meme's hateful intent, as it dehumanizes Muslims by associating them with an animal commonly viewed as impure or offensive in Western contexts."@en .
_:Nc377f824494647ec96829e84fcf437eb <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualMaterial> .
_:N762d11719dc94b1d9b8daca4a5e0679c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01475#stereotype_vlad_the_impaler_as_fantasy_monster> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A modern cultural stereotype that portrays Vlad the Impaler as a fictional monster or villain, often in popular media (e.g., 'Dracula' myths, though Vlad was not Dracula). The meme uses this stereotype to create a grotesque, fantastical image of Vlad as a 'forest of poles' to exaggerate his brutality and associate it with Muslims."@en .
_:N292f03a24fe24581bf06375206957c70 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:N541f0cb331d74b24b8148b8a45b435b6 .
