<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01295#cyberbullying> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme is a form of cyberbullying as it attacks a specific group (clergy) based on their identity and role, and it is abusive in its implication of widespread criminal behavior. The meme is also cyberbullying as it attacks a specific group (transgender people) by using the term 'transgender' in a derogatory and misleading way. This is a form of hate speech and cyberbullying."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01475#stereotype_vlad_the_impaler_as_barbaric> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A historical stereotype that portrays Vlad the Impaler as an extreme, brutal, and monstrous figure, often used in popular culture and memes to represent violence and cruelty. The meme exploits this stereotype by associating him with the fictionalized 'Muslim invasion' narrative to create a hateful caricature."@en .
_:N7e365d6a6a524b4db888a45da78e2332 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
