<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01293#mapping_001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The gross, unclean hand is mapped onto the consequence of forgetting to wash hands"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#horizontallyAdjacentTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> _:N2cbc5c270f564778823988e65ca09778 .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01452#mapping_id_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The visual entity 'chimp' is mapped onto the textual concept 'the feeling after a long day at work'. The chimp's relaxed, slightly slumped posture with one arm draped over its body and the other resting on its knee is humorously equated to human exhaustion after a long workday. This is an anthropomorphized representation where the chimp's physical state serves as a visual metaphor for the textual description of post-work fatigue. The mapping is established through the direct juxtaposition of the text overlay with the chimp's posture, creating a clear analogical relationship where the chimp embodies the feeling described in the text."@en .
_:Nbf5e48d3ae764a78abb991c1cd3ada9d <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01274#self_perception_vs_others_view> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A social and psychological concept that underpins the meme's structure. It refers to the idea that individuals often perceive themselves differently from how others perceive them. In this meme, the contrast is used humorously or ironically to suggest that someone who thinks they look ordinary is perceived as intimidating or dangerous by a specific group ('pados wale pandit jee'). This concept requires external knowledge of social dynamics and humor to be fully understood."@en .
_:N1e348d25eab048b0bba4b6e989ea50c0 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
