<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01235#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the protagonist of the meme's text, who is experiencing intense sexual desire ('feeling horny asf') but is unable to pursue it due to their partner's menstrual cycle. The user identifies with this first-person scenario, imagining themselves in this situation. The visual material of the man with an enthusiastic expression and open-handed gesture is mapped onto this protagonist, representing the user's emotional state and decision-making process. The text explicitly uses 'you' ('your habibi') which directly projects the user onto the described situation."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#AnalogicalMapping> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#perimeterFraming> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> _:Ne830d51ec8b54e80a15084ceccab483a .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01436#toxicity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The quality of being harmful or damaging, especially in the context of social or psychological harm. The meme is toxic because it trivializes a serious and traumatic event, potentially normalizing or mocking the suffering of autistic individuals, and reinforces harmful narratives."@en .
_:N1f61e6b124464893a77b544af0dbd3fe <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
