_:Ncf0e5cd3fc9c4929b222701a2e275adf <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01379#propaganda_through_emotional_appeal> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#BackgroundKnowledge> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01475#mapping_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Muslims are mapped onto Vlad the Impaler"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01275#assertion_about_01275> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general#hasToxicityExplanation> "The meme uses a confrontational visual of a Black man shouting at a press conference to dismiss a perceived threat or criticism, potentially reinforcing harmful stereotypes about Black men being aggressive or authoritative. The text 'voetsek!!!' (Afrikaans for 'go away') is used to forcefully reject the idea that 't willl stop eating palony and viannas', which could be interpreted as mocking or dismissing specific individuals or entities. While the intent may be satirical or ironic, the combination of the visual and text can activate harmful stereotypes and potentially cause offense or harm to the targeted individuals or communities."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01276#concept_nonverbal_communication> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This refers to the process of conveying messages without using words, through body language, facial expressions, gestures, and tone of voice. It is a fundamental aspect of human interaction and is widely studied in fields like psychology, sociology, and communication studies. The meme relies on this concept to argue that a smile, as a non-verbal cue, can be more impactful than words."@en .
_:N926cf7493dde440ebc932d419785d7df <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01379#western_media_representation_of_africa> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The tendency in Western media to portray Africa through a narrow, often negative, lens that emphasizes poverty, conflict, and need for aid, while ignoring the continent's diversity, complexity, and agency. This representation can contribute to a distorted global understanding of Africa and its people."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#backgroundPreserving> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates one element placed only over neutral areas to preserve important content of another dimension.\nE.g. text placed only over neutral areas to preserve important visual content in memes"@en .
_:N795b59c5204d45089095eba798b1c67a <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
