<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01483#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: feeling_bored_let_s_go_to_a_mosque; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a group of men, mostly wearing white traditional attire and head coverings, seated in what appears to be a mosque during a religious gathering or prayer. The central figure, an older man with a white cap, is shown with a bored or disinterested expression, resting his head on his hand. The overlaid text reads, \"feeling bored, let's go to a mosque.\" The overall intent of this meme is to use the juxtaposition of the visual of people in a religious setting with the text to create a humorous or ironic commentary on the idea of boredom being alleviated by religious activity. The meme does not contain abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or propaganda elements. It is a lighthearted, satirical meme that relies on the contrast between the solemnity of the setting and the mundane, humorous text to generate a comedic effect. The visual elements do not activate any toxic stereotypes or harmful combinations, as the image is not targeting any specific group based on protected characteristics, and the humor is not directed at any community or individual. The meme's intent is to entertain through irony and situational humor, not to cause harm or promote negative stereotypes."@en .
