<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01395#mapping_001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The text 'i just found out mexican babies come out just like the food' creates an analogical mapping where the visual of a woman in labor (representing the physical act of childbirth) is mapped onto the concept of 'Mexican babies coming out'. The text uses the intense, dramatic visual of childbirth to metaphorically represent the 'coming out' of Mexican babies, linking the physical process to a cultural stereotype about Mexican food being 'spicy'. This mapping is offensive as it reduces a complex cultural identity to a crude, food-based joke."@en .
