_:N077b1b50818b480d89e8b9f5c99a74da <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01439#audience_id> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme is designed for a broad, general internet audience familiar with internet humor, visual puns, and common idioms. It relies on cultural knowledge of the idiom 'get the goat' and the ability to appreciate absurd wordplay and visual juxtaposition, which are common elements in meme culture. There are no specific demographic, cultural, or community markers that target a narrow group; the humor is accessible to anyone who understands the basic English idiom and can interpret the visual pun. The meme is lighthearted and non-toxic, making it suitable for a wide range of users without requiring specific background knowledge beyond general internet literacy."@en .
_:N454f6f05139048a6960f69cfe4b951e4 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:N49aa778753cf4b71bcc6d1b26e982ea1 .
_:N15512a982624488daf2b00049c33b602 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01274#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a man in a beanie and leather jacket with a stern, confrontational expression, juxtaposed with text that reads 'how you guys think you looks like' and 'but when pados wale pandit jee sees you'. The term 'pados wale pandit jee' is a derogatory and stereotypical reference to certain Indian political or religious figures, often used in a mocking or demeaning manner. The overall intent is to mock or ridicule individuals who are perceived as being overly confident or self-important, by implying that they appear ordinary to others but are viewed as threatening or intimidating by certain groups. This meme uses a visual of a serious-looking man to symbolize the perceived 'dangerous' or 'intimidating' view held by the 'pados wale pandit jee'. The meme is not explicitly abusive or hateful towards a specific protected group, but it does contain elements of harmful stereotyping and potential cyberbullying, as it uses derogatory language to mock a specific group of people. The intent is to create a humorous or ironic effect by contrasting the viewer's self-perception with the perceived view of others, but it does so in a way that could be seen as demeaning or disrespectful to the group being referenced."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#DramaticIrony> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One dimension revealing information another dimension does not provide in memes, e.g. text revealing information visuals don't show"@en .
