<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01465#assertion_about_01465> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general#asserts> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01465#hateful_divisiveness> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01459#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman sitting in a corner of a white room, visibly distressed and surrounded by numerous spiders. The text overlay reads 'trust me... they're re all terrorists.' The meme uses the visual of a person in fear of spiders (arachnophobia) to create a humorous or ironic juxtaposition with the absurd claim that all spiders are terrorists. The overall intent is to satirize or mock the idea of overgeneralization or paranoia, particularly in the context of labeling all members of a group (spiders) as dangerous or evil. The meme does not target any specific human group based on protected characteristics, nor does it contain abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynistic, or propaganda content. The humor stems from the absurdity of the claim, not from any harmful stereotype or attack on a community. The visual elements (spiders, woman's fearful expression) are used to create a relatable scenario for those who fear spiders, and the text is used to subvert expectations for comedic effect."@en .
_:N9ac56c84b7d94bce8cbbf959d59776f3 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:N7bf95268759b4b3b8032fa3b98b80e32 .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01329#man_on_right> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An older Caucasian man wearing a light-colored cowboy hat and a green button-up shirt, holding a revolver with both hands and aiming it forward. He has a weathered face, a watch on his left wrist, and is seated in what appears to be a vehicle. His expression is serious and focused. This is a central visual element, conveying aggression and confrontation."@en .
