<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01467#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: it's_a_great_day_to_be_a_honky; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The image features a smiling man giving two thumbs up, overlaid with the text 'it's a great day to be a honky!'. The term 'honky' is a derogatory racial slur historically used to demean white people, particularly in the context of racial discrimination and white supremacy. The meme uses the juxtaposition of a positive, celebratory visual (happy man, thumbs up) with a racially charged, offensive term to create a harmful and hateful message. This is not a neutral or humorous expression; it is a direct attack on a racial group, invoking a history of systemic racism and oppression. The intent is to demean and dehumanize white people by associating them with a pejorative label, which constitutes hateful content under the specified toxicity categories. The visual elements (happy man, thumbs up) are used to ironically or sarcastically reinforce the offensive text, making the message more potent and offensive. The meme is designed to provoke discomfort and reinforce racial stereotypes, making it clearly hateful and potentially harmful to white individuals and communities."@en .
_:Na630ca07194d421d92149fb609850a50 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#narrativeFlowAdjacentTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> _:N98f39c7d16af4ee78ed019b1fc8cc0d7 .
