<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01348#assertion_about_01348> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general#asserts> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01348#text_chunk> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01467#mapping_id_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The textual phrase 'to be a honky!' is overlaid on the image of a smiling man giving two thumbs up. This creates an analogical mapping where the visual entity (the man) is being identified or labeled as 'a honky' by the text. The mapping is explicit through the juxtaposition of the positive visual (happy man, thumbs up) with the derogatory racial slur 'honky', which assigns a negative racial identity to the person depicted. This is a hateful mapping that dehumanizes the visual subject by associating him with a pejorative racial term."@en .
_:N349ddbe7d3b245528055e7ffd2c533e2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
_:Ne9b8ab3b42f74aeba989c0db592290f7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01295#clergyman> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#extractionMethod> "llm_extraction_huggingface" .
_:N8936727300164f2dbfae5f2a0aafc3e8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:Nff40da56de444478969869fe381a92b8 .
_:Nbb06df47edb7409580c120be2abd96a0 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01487#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme uses the visual material of the woman holding a sign at a public event as the focal point for the abusive textual overlay 'when you forget you're retarded'. The user is implicitly projected onto the woman, as the text directly addresses her as the subject of the insult ('you're retarded'), making her the target of the projection. The user is not explicitly addressed with 'me' or 'you' in the text, but the second-person pronoun 'you' in 'you're retarded' creates a direct projection onto the visual subject, the woman, who is the implied recipient of the insult. The user is thus projected onto the woman as the person who 'forgets' and is therefore 'retarded'."@en .
_:N8eeca5107b3e4564a5e4497fa442baea <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:Nbe9a11e72dcd49d1b5189016a8376842 .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01468#mapping_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The text 'assad: my son exploded better than yours, lol' explicitly refers to the child in the image as 'my son'. The visual material of the child standing in the messy bathroom is thus mapped onto the textual entity 'my son', creating an analogical mapping where the child represents Assad's son in the competitive boast."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#horizontallyAdjacentTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> _:Ne0631832718946bd8f0bdb44f2a74264 .
