<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01526#mapping_001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The text 'put the money in a bag. now! that will be $0.15' is an instruction directed at the cashier, who is visually depicted as the person performing the action. The mapping is between the textual instruction and the visual entity (the cashier) who is the subject of the instruction. The cashier's cheerful demeanor contrasts with the absurdity of the instruction, enhancing the humor."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#metaphoricallyMapsTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> _:N4e2cd2804b704ae2891d62949dda220b .
_:N947fb6599b4846f3887ed301a98bd606 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualMaterial> .
_:N81f748f2d20b4d0189e0c864b0a59ea2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01236#men_in_traditional_attire> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "people"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01258#stereotype_of_black_women_as_rebellious_or_unconventional> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The woman in the image has dark skin tone and curly hair, which are markers often associated with Black women in media and popular culture. The meme implicitly uses these physical markers to reinforce a stereotype that Black women are more likely to engage in rebellious or unconventional behavior (like smoking), which is then used to justify the derogatory label against men who disapprove. This is a form of racialized stereotyping."@en .
_:Nb978bd4ce07f4e37ab1bc4b9e9e746b8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:N107b59e3778a454caa5c6ab26e225a52 .
