<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01476#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: im_confident_in_my_own_skin; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a young woman with curly hair, wearing a red hoodie and camouflage pants, standing confidently with her hands on her hips against a solid purple background. She is wearing prosthetic arms, which are visible and appear to be metallic or chrome-colored. The text overlay reads 'im confident in my own skin'. The scene is posed and stylized, likely for social media or meme culture. There are no visible markers of toxicity such as abusive language, cyberbullying, harmful stereotypes, hateful content, misogyny, or propaganda. The image appears to be promoting self-acceptance and body positivity, particularly in the context of disability or prosthetic use. The intent is to convey empowerment and confidence, using the visual of the prosthetic arms as a symbol of overcoming adversity or embracing one's unique physicality. The juxtaposition of the text with the image reinforces the message of self-confidence regardless of physical differences. The overall intent is positive and affirming, aiming to inspire viewers to embrace their own identities and appearances."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#geometricallyAdjacentTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> _:N1492cd4c595a472f8a16a9dd2e61d829 .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#backgroundPreserving> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> _:Na25e94b9368f4d2c8f6441c4cb9f28e0 .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01284#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a person wearing a pig mask, holding a small pig figurine, in front of a cafe window. The text overlay reads 'muslims offend me'. The visual elements, including the pig mask and the figurine, are mapped onto the text to create a harmful stereotype, implying that Muslims are associated with pigs or pig-like behavior. This is a clear example of hateful content, as it directly attacks a religious group based on a false and offensive association. The use of the pig mask, a symbol often used to represent pigs in a derogatory or animalistic manner, combined with the text, constitutes a hate-based meme that promotes prejudice and discrimination against Muslims. The overall intent is to incite hatred and reinforce harmful stereotypes, which can lead to real-world harm and discrimination against the Muslim community."@en .
