<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01452#work_exhaustion_stereotype> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme relies on the universal human experience of post-work fatigue, which is a common social and cultural phenomenon. It implicitly references the widespread understanding that people experience physical and mental exhaustion after long workdays, often leading to a desire to relax or 'chill out'. This stereotype is not harmful as it is broadly relatable and non-discriminatory."@en .
