<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01324#audience_id> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The target audience for this meme is individuals familiar with 1960s British culture and the historical event known as 'The Great Train Robbery'. The meme relies on the audience's recognition of this specific criminal event and its cultural legacy to generate humor through ironic juxtaposition. The intended community includes internet meme users who understand the conventions of visual humor, particularly those who appreciate absurdist or satirical content that plays on incongruity. The meme's effectiveness depends on the audience's ability to recognize the contrast between the mundane appearance of the men (holding books, casual attire) and the dramatic, criminal connotation of the label 'the great train robbers'. This suggests the target community is likely composed of adults with some exposure to British history, media, or internet meme culture, who can appreciate the comedic effect of mislabeling ordinary people as infamous criminals."@en .
