<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01459#person> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme is designed for a general audience familiar with arachnophobia and the concept of absurd humor. The target community includes individuals who recognize the visual trope of a person in fear of spiders and appreciate the comedic juxtaposition with the overgeneralization of 'terrorists'. The humor relies on understanding the logical fallacy of overgeneralization and the absurdity of applying human-centric terms like 'terrorist' to non-human entities. The target audience is not specific to any protected demographic or community, but rather those who can engage with the meme's satirical intent and find the irony amusing."@en .
