<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01349#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the textual material 'girl you're so special' and 'i'm gonna give you a gold star', and the scene of the affectionate interaction. The text uses second-person address ('you'), directly implicating the viewer in the interaction. The user is positioned as the recipient of the affectionate message, creating a direct semiotic projection onto the scene and text. This projection is harmful as it invites the user to imagine themselves in the role of the girl being addressed by Hitler, thereby internalizing the sanitized, affectionate narrative that trivializes his historical atrocities."@en .
