<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01359#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: area_51_naruto_runners_meme; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts a sequence of three images: a man with an afro hairstyle yelling in a desert, a man in a suit holding a microphone yelling 'let me iiiiiiiiiiiin!', and a gate with the text 'let me in'. The text 'naruto runners' is overlaid on both the first and second images. The overall intent is to humorously suggest that 'Naruto Runners' (a fictional or meme-based concept) are trying to enter 'Area 51' or a similar restricted location, with the final image of the gate symbolizing the barrier they are attempting to breach. The meme is intended to be comedic and satirical, playing on the absurdity of the scenario. There is no abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or propaganda content present. The visual elements do not contain any toxic markers or stereotypes. The intent is purely for entertainment and humor, using juxtaposition to create a funny narrative about fictional characters trying to access a secret or restricted area."@en .
_:Nd68a83d4401642caae36b40f8917aeb3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01465#audience_id> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The intended audience is individuals who may be susceptible to divisive messaging, particularly those exposed to or influenced by stereotypes associating Muslims with terrorism. The meme targets viewers who might be primed to accept simplistic, inflammatory narratives that exploit religious markers (niqab) and violent symbolism (bomb props) to promote prejudice or justify discrimination against Muslims. The text 'dont get confused' suggests the meme is designed to manipulate viewers into accepting a false dichotomy, making it especially targeted at audiences that may lack critical engagement with complex social issues or are influenced by media that reinforces harmful stereotypes."@en .
_:N99c272ff7acf4ea9bea71aca8cb4f22b <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:Ne7c704672e294811b46dd40d59e6e715 .
_:N78d338a0aaed4cabb8041a3bc7f4e800 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01256#abortion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The medical procedure to terminate a pregnancy. This is a real-world concept and a sensitive, often controversial, topic. The text references abortion, which is a real-world event and concept that is central to the meme's scenario."@en .
_:Nb6ff1303cca64feba9a14d905e30445c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
