<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01379#assertion_about_01379> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general#hasToxicityExplanation> "The meme perpetuates harmful stereotypes by framing the interaction as a 'visit' to 'the children of Africa,' which reinforces the 'white savior' narrative and exoticizes the African child. This can lead to a distorted understanding of global inequality and cultural contexts, ignoring the agency of the child and potentially encouraging viewers to support charitable causes without critically examining the underlying power dynamics."@en .
