<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01324#criminal_stereotype> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The stereotype that associates certain physical appearances or behaviors with criminality. The meme plays on this by labeling ordinary-looking men as 'the great train robbers', creating an absurd contrast. This stereotype is a real-world concept that the meme implicitly references to generate humor through incongruity. The meme's effectiveness depends on the audience's understanding of how such stereotypes are typically applied in media and popular culture."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01524#dark_comedy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme employs dark humor, which is a comedic style that derives its effect from subjects that are taboo, morbid, or potentially offensive (e.g., violence, death, or betrayal). Understanding this genre is necessary to interpret the meme's intent as a joke rather than a literal threat, even though the visual content is alarming."@en .
