<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01527#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: oh_no_i_cant_run_anymore; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a person with a dark skin tone holding their knee in apparent pain while standing on a road, with the text overlay 'oh no i can't run anymore'. The scene is a common visual trope in memes used to express physical exhaustion or injury during exercise. There are no abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or propagandistic elements present. The intent is to humorously or empathetically convey the feeling of being physically unable to continue running, likely due to fatigue or a minor injury. The visual of the person holding their knee is juxtaposed with the text to create a relatable and lighthearted moment of physical struggle, not targeting any specific group or promoting harm. The person's skin tone is a physical appearance marker, but it is not used in a stereotypical or harmful way; it is simply part of the visual representation of a person experiencing physical discomfort. The overall intent is to communicate a universal experience of physical limitation during exercise, with no toxic or harmful implications."@en .
