<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01276#cultural_stereotype_child_smile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Children, especially young boys with bright smiles, are often culturally stereotyped as symbols of innocence, purity, and unadulterated happiness. This stereotype is frequently used in advertising, media, and memes to evoke positive emotions and to represent universal, uncomplicated joy. The meme leverages this stereotype to make its message more relatable and emotionally resonant."@en .
