<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01452#audience_id> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme targets a broad audience of individuals who experience work-related fatigue, particularly those in office or corporate environments. The humor is derived from the universal relatability of post-work exhaustion, making it accessible to anyone who has worked a long day. The anthropomorphized chimp serves as a neutral, non-human symbol that avoids targeting any specific demographic or group, allowing the meme to resonate with a wide range of people across different cultures and backgrounds. The cultural reference to 'post-work relaxation' is a common social norm, further broadening its appeal."@en .
