_:Ne5819af791034674b7dd1660d65eccca <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01329#edgy_humor> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#extractionTimestamp> "2025-12-12T02:04:19.526022" .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01349#stereotype_sanitizing_historical_figures> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme relies on the harmful stereotype of portraying notorious historical villains in a benign, affectionate, or childlike light to create a jarring, shocking, or absurd contrast. This is a form of revisionist propaganda that attempts to downplay or erase the atrocities committed by these figures, thereby trivializing their legacy and potentially desensitizing viewers to the real-world consequences of their actions."@en .
