<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01293#mapping_001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The visual material of the hand covered in a thick, dark, viscous substance is mapped onto the textual concept of 'forgetting to wash your hands'. The image uses the hand as a visual metaphor for the unpleasant outcome of neglecting a basic hygiene task. The text explicitly states the cause ('when you forget to wash your hands'), and the visual material represents the effect (the dirty, dripping hand). This is a direct analogical mapping where the visual entity (dirty hand) is the embodiment of the textual concept (neglecting handwashing)."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01379#white_savior_narrative> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A cultural trope in Western media and philanthropy where a white person, often from a developed country, is portrayed as coming to 'save' or 'help' people from a non-Western or impoverished context, often implying a power imbalance and exoticizing the local people. This narrative is often criticized for reinforcing colonialist attitudes and ignoring the agency of the people being 'saved'."@en .
