<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01392#audience_id> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme is designed for individuals within Christian communities who are familiar with the phrase 'hello jesus' and the concept of divine intervention ('thanks for making a way!'). The humor relies on the juxtaposition of a casual phone call with a religious invocation, which is a culturally specific reference rooted in Christian expressions of gratitude and faith. The target audience is expected to understand and appreciate this religious-cultural pun, making it most effective for Christians, particularly those in Western contexts where such phrases are common in everyday speech and prayer. The visual of a cheerful, relatable young girl enhances the lighthearted, non-threatening tone, making it accessible to a broad Christian demographic, including youth and families."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01452#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "User projected onto the chimp's exhausted posture as a representation of post-work fatigue"@en .
