<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01349#audience_id> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The target community for this meme is individuals who are familiar with historical figures like Adolf Hitler and the Holocaust, and who may be exposed to internet memes that use shock value or absurd juxtaposition to provoke reactions. The meme is designed to appeal to an audience that understands the historical context of Hitler's atrocities but may be drawn to the provocative, ironic, or darkly humorous nature of the image. This audience likely engages with internet culture that includes satirical, revisionist, or edgy content, and may be seeking to shock, provoke, or challenge conventional historical narratives. The meme's harmful intent suggests it targets users who are either unaware of its dangerous implications or who are deliberately engaging with it for its provocative nature, potentially normalizing or trivializing genocide through absurd contrast."@en .
