<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01269#kermit_waving_scene> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Kermit the Frog is seated on a white block, waving with one hand while smiling. The scene is framed to focus on his expressive gesture and cheerful demeanor."@en .
_:Nc4b799953c5c4b3ba0cacb803287e83e <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01527#running_as_exercise> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#relatedTo> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01527#text_chunk> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01349#text_chunk_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Text content: 'girl you're so special'. Position: top center of the image, above the man's head."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01379#toxicity_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme perpetuates harmful stereotypes by framing the interaction as a 'visit' to 'the children of Africa,' which reinforces the 'white savior' narrative and exoticizes the African child. This can lead to a distorted understanding of global inequality and cultural contexts, ignoring the agency of the child and potentially encouraging viewers to support charitable causes without critically examining the underlying power dynamics."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01389#person> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A person wearing a grey hoodie with the hood up, holding a cat close to their face. Their eyes are closed and they have a gentle smile, suggesting affection or contentment. The person's face is partially obscured by the hood and the cat. The hoodie appears to be a standard casual sweatshirt with a visible patch on the sleeve."@en .
