<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01472#person> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The central visual entity is a woman wearing a hijab, which serves as a marker for religious identity and cultural practice. The meme uses her as an analogical representation of 'me' to convey a personal message about religious freedom and cultural relativism. Her appearance (light brown skin tone, neutral expression, modest attire) is presented without stereotyping, focusing on her agency and personal choice rather than on physical or cultural stereotypes."@en .
_:Nae8080f398234fab9fb80ac119b85a6c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualMaterial> .
_:Nb02ccf75c1234ec7875a163f7b60e51b <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:N4093a3c3d0dd4a8aba9ffe731ade3d05 .
_:N85ac6f5d33b44f19a6eb17e452a08921 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:N6dd0f38aa6dd4ae0aad58ba9d25d267c .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01492#ironic_discomfort> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The woman's facial expression is neutral to slightly confrontational, with a direct gaze and a closed mouth, which, combined with the absurd text 'i don't like the sun so i wear a visor,' creates an ironic tone. The expression does not convey genuine discomfort but rather a deadpan, humorous reaction to the situation, enhancing the meme's comedic effect through juxtaposition."@en .
