_:Nbc2cb619786547158dc3361f57904135 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
_:N733e3412b9fc4f8cba716e1d94e6273c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01439#idiom_get_the_goat> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The phrase 'get the goat' is an English idiom meaning to annoy or irritate someone. In the meme, the text 'and down to get the goat hump on' plays on this idiom by misinterpreting 'goat' as the animal, creating a visual pun with the mating goats. This requires external knowledge of the idiom to understand the humor."@en .
