<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01274#semiotic_projection_2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is also implicitly projected onto the scene's implied perspective of 'pados wale pandit jee' as seen in the bottom text ('but when pados wale pandit jee sees you'). While the text does not directly address 'you' in the second clause, the contrastive structure ('how you guys think... but when...') creates a dual projection: the user is first projected onto the self-perception (the man), and then the user is implied to be the subject of the external judgment (the 'pados wale pandit jee' view). The user is thus projected onto the scene's implied external judgment, which is embodied by the man's stern expression."@en .
