<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01498#audience_id> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The target community is individuals familiar with U.S. political discourse, particularly those engaged in debates around immigration policy (DACA), historical accountability (slavery), and racialized historical narratives. The meme is designed to provoke a reaction from viewers who understand the political positions of the Democratic Party and the moral implications of historical responsibility, especially those who are sensitive to or concerned about racialized historical arguments. The use of a shocked woman as a visual proxy suggests the meme is aimed at an audience that interprets such expressions as indicators of moral outrage or disbelief, likely those who are politically active or socially conscious about issues of justice and historical legacy."@en .
