<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01467#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the visual material of the man (the smiling man giving two thumbs up) through the textual overlay 'to be a honky!'. The meme explicitly maps the man as 'a honky', creating a semiotic projection where the viewer is invited to identify with or associate themselves with the man as a member of the targeted racial group. This projection is not deictic (e.g., 'you' or 'me') but is implied through the hateful mapping and the user's identification with the visual subject as the target of the slur. The projection is onto the VisualMaterial entity 'man' via the TextualMaterial 'text_chunk_1' (specifically the phrase 'to be a honky!'), which assigns a racial identity to the visual subject, thereby projecting the user onto that identity."@en .
