<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01392#divine_intervention_stereotype> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The phrase 'thanks for making a way!' implicitly references the stereotype or cultural trope of divine intervention, where God or Jesus is believed to miraculously solve problems or create opportunities. This concept is deeply embedded in Christian faith and popular media, often portrayed in movies, songs, and everyday speech as a source of hope or explanation for unexpected successes. The meme uses this concept humorously by juxtaposing it with a mundane activity (a phone call), creating a comedic contrast."@en .
