<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01498#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the visual material of the woman displaying a shocked or incredulous facial expression. This projection is implicit, as the meme uses her exaggerated reaction to visually represent the viewer's supposed reaction to the provocative rhetorical question in the text. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the framing of the scene and the rhetorical nature of the text create an implicit identification with the viewer's emotional response, making the woman's expression a stand-in for the user's projected disbelief."@en .
