<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01392#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: hello_jesus_meme; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a young Black girl smiling while holding a phone to her ear, with text overlay reading 'hello jesus' and 'thanks for making a way!'. The scene is innocent and appears to be a lighthearted, humorous take on a common phrase used in Christian contexts, particularly in reference to divine intervention or miracles. The girl's appearance, including her curly hair and skin tone, is not being used to stereotype or demean; rather, she is presented as a relatable, cheerful character engaging in a common activity (talking on the phone). There is no abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or propagandistic intent. The meme's intent is to create a humorous juxtaposition between the casual, modern act of calling someone on the phone and the religious invocation of Jesus, implying a playful or ironic tone. The visual elements (the girl's appearance, clothing, and expression) are not being used to reinforce harmful stereotypes or to target any specific group. The overall intent is to entertain through a simple, relatable, and non-offensive religious pun, without any toxic or harmful implications."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01269#Kermit_the_Frog> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "fictional character"@en .
