<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01327#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projecting themselves onto the Joker character, using the character's iconic, menacing, and morally ambiguous persona to represent their own self-identification as 'twisted' rather than 'sick'. The text 'i'm not sick, i'm twisted' explicitly uses the first-person pronoun 'i', which directly deictically points to the user. The visual material of the Joker is used as a symbolic vessel for this self-identification, creating a direct analogical mapping where the user sees themselves in the Joker's persona. The projection is onto the VisualMaterial entity 'Joker' and the TextualMaterial entity 'top_text', as the user identifies with both the visual representation and the self-referential statement."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#CausalRelation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One dimension being causally related with another in memes, e.g. text explaining why visual situation exists"@en .
