<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01382#reproductive_rights> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The concept that individuals have the right to make autonomous decisions about their own reproductive health, including the right to access abortion services. This is a central theme in the meme, as the phrase 'my body my choice' is a well-known slogan associated with the pro-choice movement. The act of erasing 'Abortion' in the image is a visual metaphor that contrasts with the pro-choice message, implying a rejection of abortion as a concept, which is contrary to the pro-choice stance."@en .
_:N6a044a930b3d4ae5af87c9f95f11c74b <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01468#assertion_about_01468> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general#asserts> <http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01468#bodily_function_stereotype> .
_:Nd90390c9d5ed4772bed01a89c9cb445e <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01329#edgy_humor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme relies on 'edgy humor' — a comedic style that uses shock value, taboo language, or controversial imagery to provoke laughter or attention. This requires background knowledge of internet meme culture and the conventions of edgy humor, which often juxtapose offensive or extreme content with mundane or wholesome visuals to create a comedic effect. The combination of cowboy imagery with vulgar language is a classic example of this."@en .
