<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01382#political_meme_format> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A common format in internet culture where a visual image is used to convey a political or ideological message, often through juxtaposition or irony. This meme uses the visual of erasing 'Abortion' to create a contrast with the pro-choice slogan 'my body my choice', which is a common rhetorical strategy in political memes to provoke thought or debate on controversial issues."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01423#intimate_posture> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The individuals are in an intimate posture, with one person curled up on top of the other, partially covering their face. This posture suggests closeness, comfort, and rest, reinforcing the theme of relaxation and intimacy."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01389#confession> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The term 'confession' is used in a religious context (e.g., in Christianity, Islam, Catholicism) to refer to the act of admitting sins to a priest or deity. In the meme, it is used ironically to describe a mundane, non-religious activity, creating humor through the juxtaposition of a serious term with a trivial one."@en .
