<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01245#boy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A young boy, likely between 8-12 years old, smiling at the camera. He has light skin, light-colored eyes, and is wearing a military-style camouflage uniform and vest. His teeth are visible and appear to be braces. He is holding his hand near his neck, and has a toy grenade attached to his vest. His expression is cheerful and confident."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01456#toxicity_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme juxtaposes the celebration of Nazi leaders with the suffering of Holocaust victims, which can cause harm by trivializing or normalizing genocide and systemic atrocities. The use of hip-hop slang ('they see them rollin.....', 'they hating...') to describe the Nazi regime's actions and the victims' suffering is deeply insensitive and potentially reductive, minimizing the gravity of historical trauma."@en .
