<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01487#person> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The target audience is individuals familiar with Howard Stern's controversial and provocative media persona, as well as those who understand the cultural context of Sirius Radio events. The meme is designed for an audience that finds humor in shock value and edgy, boundary-pushing content, often associated with Stern's show. The use of the term 'retarded' as a punchline implies the audience is aware of its offensive nature and may be engaging with the meme as a form of dark humor or satire, likely within online communities that appreciate or are accustomed to such abrasive content. The audience is likely to be adults who consume media that challenges social norms and may have a tolerance for offensive language, even if it is harmful."@en .
