<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01236#isis_strip_club_scene> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A fictional, satirical, and offensive concept implying that ISIS members are attending or reacting to a strip club. This is a harmful stereotype that falsely associates ISIS with sexualized, vulgar, and inappropriate behavior, which is not only inaccurate but also dehumanizing and potentially inciting hatred or violence against a specific group. The concept relies on the real-world entity 'ISIS' (Islamic State of Iraq and Syria), a terrorist organization, and the cultural phenomenon of 'strip clubs' to create a toxic and harmful joke."@en .
