<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01348#audience_id> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme is designed to target and mock men in traditional Muslim attire, particularly those wearing white turbans and traditional garments, by implying they are patrons of a sexually suggestive or inappropriate 'strip club' scenario. This is achieved through the juxtaposition of sheep with their rear ends facing forward (a visual often used in memes to imply absurdity or sexualization) and the exaggerated shock expressions of the men, who are portrayed as reacting to this scene. The meme relies on harmful stereotypes that portray Muslim men as sexually promiscuous, animalistic, or inappropriate in public spaces, which is a form of cultural and religious mockery aimed at this specific community."@en .
