_:N0c7607f4e0a44673bb84eafc50d519b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01487#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: when_you_forget_youre_retarded.jpg; hasOverallIntent: Abusive; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman at a Howard Stern Sirius Radio event, holding a sign with the date '1-9-06'. The overlaid text reads 'when you forget you're retarded'. This meme uses a juxtaposition of a public figure in a professional setting with a derogatory and demeaning insult. The intent is to mock or insult someone who forgets something, using the term 'retarded' which is a harmful and offensive slur historically used to demean people with intellectual disabilities. The meme is abusive as it targets an individual with a degrading label, potentially threatening or humiliating them. The visual context (a public event, a professional setting) contrasts with the crude insult, amplifying the insult's impact. The meme's intent is to provoke laughter or shock through the use of a harmful and outdated term, which can cause emotional harm and perpetuate stigma against people with disabilities."@en .
