<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01324#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is not explicitly projected onto any specific element via deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you'. However, the meme's overall intent creates an implicit projection where the viewer (user) is invited to imagine themselves as part of the group or to identify with the humorous juxtaposition. The projection is onto the scene of the group of men holding books, as the text 'the great train robbers' labels them, prompting the user to engage with the absurdity of the label applied to ordinary-looking individuals. The user is thus projected onto the scene entity, which serves as the focal point for the meme's ironic commentary."@en .
