<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01382#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a hand using chalk to strike through the word 'Abortion' on a green chalkboard, with the text 'my body my choice' overlaid at the top. The scene visually represents the act of erasing or rejecting the concept of abortion, while the text asserts a pro-choice stance. The overall intent is to communicate a political or ideological message supporting reproductive rights, specifically the right to choose whether or not to have an abortion. This is a common meme format used to express support for abortion access as a fundamental personal right. There is no abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or propaganda intent in this image. The visual metaphor of erasing 'Abortion' juxtaposed with the slogan 'my body my choice' serves to frame abortion as something to be rejected or removed from consideration, which is contrary to the pro-choice message. The meme's intent is to provoke thought or debate on reproductive rights, and while it may be controversial, it does not target any specific group with abuse or hate. The image does not contain any qua-entities that would activate stereotypes or toxic associations."@en .
