<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01324#the_great_train_robbers> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A notorious real-world criminal event in the United Kingdom, where a gang of 15 men robbed a train carrying £2.6 million in cash, which was intended for the British government. The robbery, which occurred on August 8, 1963, is one of the most infamous crimes in British history. The term 'the great train robbers' refers to the actual gang members involved in this heist. The meme uses this historical reference to create a humorous contrast between the mundane appearance of the men in the photo and the dramatic, criminal connotation of the label, implying they are being portrayed as infamous criminals."@en .
