<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01329#aggression> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The man on the right is holding a revolver and aiming it forward with a serious, focused expression, conveying a sense of aggression and confrontation. The text 'saddle up motherfuckers' reinforces this aggressive tone."@en .
_:N3a9088293b4e413d8318f980ebd4e38f <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01349#stereotype_trivializing_genocide> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#extractionTimestamp> "2025-12-12T02:08:28.596174" .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#narrativeFlowAdjacentTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> _:N0549ee881b9c4aeeb64733d39878e190 .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01275#anger> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The man's facial expression, with furrowed brows, wide-open mouth, and strained look, combined with his aggressive shouting and pointing gesture, clearly conveys intense anger or defiance. This is reinforced by the confrontational context of a press conference and the dismissive text overlay."@en .
_:N33286f82d5254c5b85e6e4b7cd616cc9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01492#stereotype_visors_as_headwear> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The visor is a type of headwear that is typically associated with sports, casual wear, or sun protection. The meme uses the visor as a visual marker to create a humorous contrast with the text, which implies that the woman is wearing it to avoid the sun. This is an exaggerated and absurd interpretation of the visor's purpose, and it relies on the viewer's understanding of the visor as a functional item for sun protection."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01274#pados_wale_pandit_jee> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#extractedFrom> "01274.png" .
_:N4e130c76fbbc4ca1a5b16e67323be88c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01247#toxicity_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme uses a historical figure associated with genocide and extreme racism to make a joke about racism, which can trivialize the suffering of victims and normalize harmful ideologies."@en .
