<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01275#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the visual scene of the Black man in a suit shouting aggressively at a press conference, with multiple microphones. This projection is implied through the confrontational and dismissive tone of the text overlay ('if you think t willl stop eating palony and viannas voetsek!!!'), which directly addresses the viewer ('you') as the one who might hold the mistaken belief. The user is thus positioned as the 'you' in the text, experiencing the emotional intensity of the scene as if they are the one being confronted or the one who is being told to 'go away'. The visual material of the man's angry expression and gesture reinforces this projection, making the user feel as though they are the target of the rejection or the one whose opinion is being forcefully dismissed."@en .
