_:Neb797da4daa048678c5c51660a74e941 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TextualMaterial> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01497#stereotype_muslims_harmful_practices> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A broader stereotype that Muslims are inherently associated with harmful or barbaric practices, which is used to justify discrimination and hatred. This stereotype is often used in conjunction with other false claims, such as the 'married to children' myth, to paint Muslims as a monolithic group of oppressors. The meme is an example of this harmful stereotype."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01465#protest_scene> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A scene depicting individuals dressed in white robes and niqabs, standing in a group during what appears to be a protest or demonstration. They are holding red flags and wearing toy-like bomb props strapped to their waists. The scene is overlaid with text that reads 'there is difference between violating muslims and other muslims' and 'dont get confused'. The individuals are positioned closely together, suggesting a collective action or demonstration."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01476#mapping_id_1> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#extractionMethod> "llm_extraction_huggingface" .
_:N9eaee1206b634ca5b799b654f8aa188a <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01274#taba_renso> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "creator or source of the meme"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01423#restful_environment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A restful environment is one that promotes relaxation, comfort, and tranquility. In the context of the meme, the setting of a bed with white linens and natural sunlight is interpreted as a restful environment, which contrasts with the implied gritty, physical nature of 'mudding'. The background knowledge required to understand the meme is that such environments are culturally associated with rest, sleep, and personal comfort, which enhances the humor of the contrast."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01475#historical_event_reconquista> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#BackgroundKnowledge> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01497#text_chunk_1> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#extractionTimestamp> "2025-12-12T02:57:31.673882" .
