<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01487#howard_stern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A famous American radio personality and media personality known for his controversial and often provocative style. The event is associated with his Sirius Radio show, which is known for its edgy and boundary-pushing content. The context of the event (a Howard Stern Sirius Radio event) is necessary to understand the setting and the nature of the public figure involved."@en .
_:N0c325341945440a7b18531b6e3b34219 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:N5123723064f84b1280081da05ea01e71 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:N57245a4ca11a4ba19a224410c74463bf .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01475#meme_scene> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A meme scene composed of a portrait of Vlad the Impaler and overlaid text that creates a hateful historical narrative. The portrait is centrally framed, and the text is arranged in three horizontal blocks above, middle, and bottom, creating a visual hierarchy that emphasizes the text's message. The scene uses the portrait as a visual anchor for the text's hateful stereotype."@en .
