<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01465#mapping_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The text 'there is difference between violating muslims and other muslims' explicitly refers to 'Muslims', which is then visually represented by the individuals wearing niqabs. The niqab is used as a qua-entity to represent 'Muslims' in a stereotypical and dehumanizing way, mapping the textual concept of 'Muslims' onto the visual depiction of these individuals. This mapping is reinforced by the context of the protest scene and the bomb props, which associate the visual representation with violence and terrorism, further solidifying the analogical link between the text and the visual material."@en .
