<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01247#Adolf_Hitler> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A black-and-white portrait of Adolf Hitler, the former Chancellor of Germany and leader of the Nazi Party. He is depicted in a military-style uniform with a strap over his shoulder, looking directly at the camera with a stern expression. His distinctive mustache and hairstyle are clearly visible. The image is a historical photograph, not a modern depiction."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01235#habibi> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An Arabic term meaning 'my beloved' or 'my darling,' commonly used in romantic or affectionate contexts. In the meme, it is used to refer to a romantic partner, specifically a woman, which is a culturally specific term that adds to the meme's context. The term is not visible in the image but is essential to understanding the relationship dynamic described in the text."@en .
