<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01469#concept_death_as_final_state> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#BackgroundKnowledge> .
_:N658b8d4d288b4b82a95cf536dda7bb6e <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01439#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the visual entity 'goat_1' (the male goat in the mating position) through the textual description 'im long and strong'. The text uses first-person pronouns ('im', a colloquial form of 'I') to create a direct identification with the goat, implying the user sees themselves as the 'long and strong' goat. This projection is onto the visual material, specifically the goat's physical form, which is being anthropomorphized with human-like qualities."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01527#mapping_id_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The text 'oh no i can't run anymore' implies a state of physical limitation or exhaustion during running. This textual concept is visually represented by the person holding their knee, a common gesture associated with pain or injury during physical activity. The mapping connects the abstract textual idea of being unable to run due to physical strain to the concrete visual depiction of someone experiencing physical discomfort, specifically at the knee. This creates an analogical mapping where the visual entity (person holding knee) serves as the instantiation of the textual concept (physical discomfort during running)."@en .
_:Nf51b43d4c0b54b6f8f3a549e34cfe4ed <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
