<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01236#dehumanization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The process of stripping away the humanity of a group or individual, often by portraying them as less than human or as objects. The meme relies on dehumanization by associating ISIS with sexualized and vulgar behavior, which is both inaccurate and harmful. This association is offensive and contributes to a hostile environment by normalizing harmful attitudes against a specific group."@en .
_:N3cf83c8190a84608a6a0c835f5051ef2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#VisualMaterial> .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#Speech-ThoughtIntegration> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01325#Soccer_Fan_Reaction> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#extractionTimestamp> "2025-12-12T02:00:26.714895" .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01268#father_daughter_bonding_concept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme relies on the universal cultural concept of father-daughter bonding, which is often idealized in media and society as a source of emotional support, love, and familial continuity. The text explicitly frames this bond as 'the best,' implying a value judgment that is culturally and socially constructed. This concept is not unique to any specific religion or culture but is presented here within a Muslim context to appeal to specific audiences."@en .
_:N1668c69a40174cb8b136c20c5ab28cf7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
